The Marlin Interface publishes a copy of all GCode commands which it sends to the MQTT Topic:

track/reporter/nn00

where nn is the NodeID

There is a Python Application called mqtt_recorder which makes it simple to subscribe to
this topic and store the GCode data in a CSV file. This is one way to record an object Path
for later editing and deployment

The mqtt_recorder is available and documented Application
https://deepwiki.com/rpdswtk/mqtt_recorder/1-overview

A typical command line is

mqtt-recorder --host 192.168.0.2 --mode record --file pathLog.csv --topic "track/reporter/2800"

